Simple reimplementation of 5x5 game found in GNU Emacs using C and Raylib.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
                    How to install (and compile)?
---------------------------------------------------------------------

    Follow instructions in INSTALL file.  You need only first 11 lines
of that GNU autogenerated prose to understand what to do.

    To compile the project, you need to have Raylib (https://www.raylib.com/)
installed on your system.  I would not talk about its installation process
because it's completely out of score of this blabbery of mine.  Refer to
Raylibs own installation instructions, or simply (like i did), install it
through a package manager.  Raylib files are found on the system by using
pkg-config.

    Note, that running yielded executable file without installing will
result in total and epic failure.  This game should be properly installed
because codebase references assets as if they were installed in pkgdatadir
(which is /usr/local/share/ttt5x5 by default).

    If for some reason, configure scripts or makefile reports need for
autoconf (or other autotool) in a clean distribution, you should report
this as a bug.  Autoconf is only required if you want to modify code in
some way, for ordinary users who just want to install a package there is
no need for that.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
                          How to contribute?
---------------------------------------------------------------------

    Found a bug --- make a bug report;
    Want more features --- make a feature request;
    Want to see your code here --- fork and do it.

    There are no documentation, there are no code guidelines, there are
no tests, there are nothing.  Don't report stupid bugs (like section titles
being misaligned in this README or something).  Those are very intended
stylistic and artistic choises made by me.

    To modify game graphics you need to have Inkscape installed.  Inkscape
project used to create assets is located in assets directory under the name
of layous.svg.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
                How to run (and compile) on Windows/NT?
---------------------------------------------------------------------

    I dunno, use MinGW (GNU-like compiler stuff), MSYS2 (whole unix-like
development environment), or something.  That if you run Windows yourself.
You can also try to cross-compile using afforementioned MinGW but that was
not tested at all. And Windows stuff also was not tested.  You're on your
own.
